import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 980 | Permanent Anti-Civilizational-Regression Mechanism · Mechanism 13 | Law-First Axiom Enshrined in the Constitution","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 980 | Permanent Anti-Civilizational-Regression Mechanism · Mechanism 13 | Law-First Axiom Enshrined in the Constitution","no":980,"module":5,"tags":["Anti-Regression","Mechanism 13","Law-First","Constitution-Enshrined","Setting Self-Consistency"],"related":["906-Law-First Principle","97-Setting-Contradiction Self-Check Table","09-Reality-as-Basis Fundamental Position"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0980_模块5-机制十三-法则优先公理入宪.md","filePath":"en/0980_模块5-机制十三-法则优先公理入宪.md"}'),s={name:"en/0980_模块5-机制十三-法则优先公理入宪.md"};function o(r,e,l,h,c,d){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-980-permanent-anti-civilizational-regression-mechanism-·-mechanism-13-law-first-axiom-enshrined-in-the-constitution" tabindex="-1">Entry 980 | Permanent Anti-Civilizational-Regression Mechanism · Mechanism 13 | Law-First Axiom Enshrined in the Constitution <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-980-permanent-anti-civilizational-regression-mechanism-·-mechanism-13-law-first-axiom-enshrined-in-the-constitution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 980 | Permanent Anti-Civilizational-Regression Mechanism · Mechanism 13 | Law-First Axiom Enshrined in the Constitution&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 906, 97, 09</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-world-s-greatest-fear-is-not-enemies-but-the-author-himself-changing-settings" tabindex="-1">Introduction: the world&#39;s greatest fear is not enemies, but the author himself changing settings <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-world-s-greatest-fear-is-not-enemies-but-the-author-himself-changing-settings" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: the world&#39;s greatest fear is not enemies, but the author himself changing settings&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilizational regression has a most special, most fatal form: the laws themselves being quietly changed. Today it is set that the strong may not revive, tomorrow the protagonist dies and the setting is changed to revive him; today it is stipulated the Great Dao is finite, tomorrow for the plot the protagonist is infinite. This kind of &quot;retcon and unfinished ending&quot; looks like merely a plot hole, but at the civilizational layer it means laws are no longer credible and Myriad Ranks lose faith in institutions. The law-first axiom enshrined in the constitution is the anti-regression system&#39;s lock that &quot;protects law itself.&quot; It ranks fifth among the six top-level axioms, enshrined with the other five: the anti-predation axiom, the republican axiom of Myriad Races, the collective-ascension axiom, the causal self-discipline axiom, and the universal equal infinite law, all built on &quot;law stable and credible.&quot; The law-first axiom requires: law comes first, never retconning, never ending unfinished; setting self-consistency above plot convenience, plot may not kidnap settings; the worldview may expand infinitely without collapse.</p><h2 id="i-mechanism-content" tabindex="-1">I. Mechanism Content <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-mechanism-content" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Mechanism Content&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Mechanism 13 stipulates: the six top-level axioms, along with all enacted laws, mechanisms, and standards, once enshrined in the constitution have supreme effect; any amendment must go through Mechanism 2&#39;s legislative procedure, and may not violate the six axioms themselves. Plot, narrative, personal cultivation insights, and temporary dispositions may in no case override law; finding law conflicts with practice, one may only amend the law itself, not bypass with &quot;this time is special.&quot;</p><h2 id="ii-operation" tabindex="-1">II. Operation <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-operation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Operation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Law-first runs by three gates:</p><ol><li><strong>Project gate</strong>: when any new mechanism, method, or civilizational project is initiated, first do a setting-self-consistency assessment; those conflicting with enacted laws are not initiated;</li><li><strong>Operation gate</strong>: finding conflict during operation, immediately freeze relevant acts, go back and amend law, forbidding &quot;do it first, talk later&quot;;</li><li><strong>Audit gate</strong>: Mechanism 4 periodically does setting-contradiction self-check (Document 97), cleaning retcon/unfinished-ending risk points.</li></ol><h2 id="iii-anti-regression-principle" tabindex="-1">III. Anti-Regression Principle <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-anti-regression-principle" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Anti-Regression Principle&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Law-changed regression is the root across Myriad Heavens and Myriad Worlds: once the author changes settings, the rules Myriad Ranks guarded before all become jokes. This mechanism&#39;s defense points:</p><ul><li><strong>Plot may not kidnap settings</strong>: however moving the plot or urgent the breakthrough, axioms and enacted laws may not be changed;</li><li><strong>Conflict only amends law</strong>: finding law conflicts with reality, what is amended is law, not quietly bypassed;</li><li><strong>Infinite expansion without collapse</strong>: the larger the worldview the more self-consistency required, and every Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm expansion passes the project gate.</li></ul><p>Old-cosmos strong ones often &quot;break settings&quot; to look awesome; the Anchor Symbiotic strong ones are precisely the opposite — truly capable ones get things done within law.</p><h2 id="iv-supervising-subjects" tabindex="-1">IV. Supervising Subjects <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-supervising-subjects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Supervising Subjects&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Law self-consistency is specifically adjudicated by Mechanism 3&#39;s Symbiotic Court axiom chamber and periodically audited by Mechanism 4; the people layer may directly report retcon/unfinished-ending on discovery; law amendments pass Anchor Council three readings, and the six axioms themselves are forever unamendable. The law network&#39;s operating state is transparent to Myriad Ranks, with all legislation and amendments fully traced on the Alaya Network, traceable, comparable, and recalculable.</p><h2 id="appendix-a-concrete-scenario-—-why-this-time-is-special-is-rejected" tabindex="-1">Appendix: A Concrete Scenario — Why &quot;This Time Is Special&quot; Is Rejected <a class="header-anchor" href="#appendix-a-concrete-scenario-—-why-this-time-is-special-is-rejected" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Appendix: A Concrete Scenario — Why &quot;This Time Is Special&quot; Is Rejected&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Some emergency boundary-breaking, with some strong one proposing: to rescue a besieged clan, temporarily bypass cross-plane reporting and directly draw origin from the nearest plane. The proposer emphasizes &quot;this time is special, saving people matters.&quot; Mechanism 3&#39;s axiom chamber replies: saving people may be done, but the process may not be bypassed — the emergency channel also exists, but it too has its own laws: report first, assess first, take minimal disturbance. &quot;Saving people&quot; that bypasses law saves this once, but harms law&#39;s forever credibility. The breakthrough finally went through the emergency channel&#39;s formal procedure, the besieged clan was saved, and law did not get a hole. However urgent the plot, law does not yield — this is what &quot;plot may not kidnap settings&quot; looks like in reality.</p><h2 id="vi-never-retcon-is-civilization-s-promise-to-myriad-ranks" tabindex="-1">VI: Never Retcon Is Civilization&#39;s Promise to Myriad Ranks <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-never-retcon-is-civilization-s-promise-to-myriad-ranks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI: Never Retcon Is Civilization&#39;s Promise to Myriad Ranks&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Law-first ultimately guards Myriad Ranks&#39; trust in institutions. When a being stakes a lifetime on cultivation, what he needs most is not talent, but certainty — certainty that the rules he guards will still be here tomorrow, certainty that the road he walks will not be voided by some temporary decision. Old-cosmos strong ones fear nothing but the author changing settings; Anchor Symbiotic Myriad Ranks fear nothing, because law has ahead of them promised &quot;I do not change.&quot; Once this promise is written into the constitution, it becomes civilization&#39;s heaviest yet most reliable foundation. Myriad Ranks may dream, cultivate, and send children into the symbiotic education system with peace of mind, because the law-earth underfoot, ten thousand years later, is still there.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: law stable and credible, Myriad Ranks need not repeatedly &quot;re-understand the world,&quot; cognitive cost approaching zero</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the predation faction wants to roam free by &quot;breaking law&quot;; law-first directly blocks this road</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type protagonists cheat via the author changing settings; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s all power is generated within stable law, never retconning</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: stable law benefits all beings, with no &quot;exception clauses&quot; based on individual strength</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the law network extends with the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm&#39;s expansion, self-consistency assessment synchronously covering</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The law-first axiom enshrined in the constitution is the anti-regression system&#39;s lock that &quot;protects the sky itself.&quot; The sky does not change lightly, and Myriad Ranks can trust the sky; once the sky is stable, civilization may expand infinitely with peace of mind.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/906_模块5-第五条-法则优先原则.html">Entry 906 · Law-First Principle</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/979_模块5-机制十二-超脱者永动建设义务.html">Entry 979 · Mechanism 12</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/97-设定矛盾自查表.html">Entry 97 · Setting-Contradiction Self-Check Table</a></li></ul>',25)])])}const g=t(s,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
